# Monte Carlo Option Pricer

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11+-blue.svg)
![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green.svg)
![Tests](https://img.shields.io/badge/tests-pytest-orange.svg)

A production-grade Monte Carlo simulation engine for pricing European options, 
with variance reduction techniques, Greeks estimation, convergence analysis, 
and an interactive visualization dashboard.

---

## 📦 Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Hrushi-0011/monte-carlo-option-pricer.git
cd monte-carlo-option-pricer
pip install -e .
```

## 🚀 Quick Start

```python
from mc_pricer.simulation import monte_carlo_price
from mc_pricer.black_scholes import black_scholes_price

# Price a European call option
price = monte_carlo_price(S=100, K=100, T=1.0, r=0.05, sigma=0.20)
print(f"Monte Carlo Price: ${price:.4f}")
```

## 📁 Project Structure

| Module | Description |
|---|---|
| `mc_pricer/simulation.py` | Geometric Brownian Motion engine |
| `mc_pricer/black_scholes.py` | Analytical Black-Scholes benchmark |
| `mc_pricer/variance_reduction.py` | Antithetic variates, control variates |
| `mc_pricer/greeks.py` | Delta, Gamma, Vega via finite differences |
| `dashboard/` | Interactive Plotly visualization dashboard |
| `notebooks/` | Jupyter notebook with theory walkthrough |
| `tests/` | Full pytest test suite |

## 🧪 Running Tests

```bash
pytest tests/ -v --cov=mc_pricer
```

## 📊 Running the Dashboard

```bash
py dashboard/app.py
```

## 📄 Report

Full methodology report available in `/report/methodology_report.md`

