## 📐 Mathematical Foundation

The pricer simulates stock prices using Geometric Brownian Motion:

$$S(T) = S(0) \cdot \exp\left[\left(r - \frac{\sigma^2}{2}\right)T + \sigma\sqrt{T}Z\right]$$

Where $Z \sim \mathcal{N}(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable.

Option price is estimated as:

$$V = e^{-rT} \cdot \mathbb{E}[\text{Payoff}(S_T)]$$
